    member 0: L ln(W/w) + sum_t E sum_j KL(P_t || nu) = 8.499640   (holds)
    member 1: L ln(W/w) + sum_t E sum_j KL(P_t || nu) = 3.053923   (holds)
    member 2: L ln(W/w) + sum_t E sum_j KL(P_t || nu) = 5.444173   (holds)
    Theorem 2.1(b): L (ln(W/w(P)) - E ln(1/w_Dn(P))) = 0.839534   (difference from the left side 4.21e-14)
  human outside the class: total probability 1.000000000000; number of data paths 6561
    left side of (0.4)  sum_t E sum_j KL(P_t || M^(t)) = 0.928985
    member 0: L ln(W/w) + sum_t E sum_j KL(P_t || nu) = 2.858029   (holds)
    member 1: L ln(W/w) + sum_t E sum_j KL(P_t || nu) = 5.225342   (holds)
  moving human (P for t <= 2, P2 after), outside: total probability 1.000000000000; number of data paths 6561
    left side of (0.4)  sum_t E sum_j KL(P_t || M^(t)) = 0.728596
    member 0: L ln(W/w) + sum_t E sum_j KL(P_t || nu) = 3.182727   (holds)
    member 1: L ln(W/w) + sum_t E sum_j KL(P_t || nu) = 5.932737   (holds)
    member 2: L ln(W/w) + sum_t E sum_j KL(P_t || nu) = 6.358473   (holds)
== C: Proposition 2.2 (K_Pi): the class {nu1, nu2, nu3, nu4}; nu3 and nu4 equal the
   human on all inputs of the scaffold, the human itself is not a member
    sum_t E Lambda(M^(t)) = 0.839534 <= L ln(W/w_Pi) = 8.499640   (holds)
== D: Theorem 3.2(b), class {P, nu1, nu2}, weights (0.05, 0.5, 0.3), n = 4
    member 1: E[G_n] = 0.996905 (<= 1);  E[sqrt(nu(D)/P(D)) prod_t 1/(1-d_t)] = 1.000000000 (= 1)
    member 2: E[G_n] = 0.994779 (<= 1);  E[sqrt(nu(D)/P(D)) prod_t 1/(1-d_t)] = 1.000000000 (= 1)
== E: Theorem 3.2(a). Scaffold: a chain of L calls; call j+1 is made only if call j
   was answered 1 (the human's answer). Class: f = 1 everywhere, and for each link j a
   member that answers 0 at link j, with weights 0.99/L each and w(f) = 0.01.
   (Exact dynamic programme over the set of unrefuted members.)
    L = 3, n =  10: max over Q of Pr[round T meets Q, no earlier question in Q] = 0.29480 at Q = ['x1'];  L/n = 0.30000   (holds)
      the same for the last mixture M^(n+1): max = 0.04730 at Q = ['x3']   (ratio to L/(n+1): 0.17)
    L = 3, n =  30: max over Q of Pr[round T meets Q, no earlier question in Q] = 0.10000 at Q = ['x1'];  L/n = 0.10000   (holds)
